      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e but it\u0027s because the picture-generator can\u0027t be a texture generator. (It needs to support generating raster data).\n\nYes. At least, not in an ergonomic sense. We don\u0027t want users to have to think too hard about \"am I going to draw this picture on a texture surface or not\".\n\n\u003e Previously, picture-backed images were lazy images.\n\nThey still are a subclass of lazy images; a subclass that gives us easier access to the picture, matrix, paint, and props. I think that\u0027s what you meant by \"texture-generating parts\", right?",
      "parentUuid": "e2ecbb99_012532e3",
