      "side": 1,
      "message": "One potential issue/inconsistency here is that skps draw themselves to a raster canvas in onGetPixels, but SkImage_Lazy::subset() [1] first tries to turn a skp into a texture-backed image, which calls `generate_picture_texture` (formerly SkPictureImageGenerator::onGenerateTexture()). I believe if an skp has a texture-backed image in it, this will result in inconsistent readbacks since this drawPicture will fail, but the `generate_picture_texture` one will succeed.\n\n\n[1] https://github.com/google/skia/blob/2a2d795fe7d085d6eb9a7b456413cb2279f7e707/src/image/SkImage_Lazy.cpp#L198",
      "revId": "75a1442c68b04f792f5898c0dc9a44fa00a79271",
